abstract: >
  SIRIUS LOCAL AI is a fully modular, offline-only AI runtime designed for secure,
  deterministic execution of commands, workflows, plugins, reasoning tasks, and
  semantic automation. Version 5.9.0 introduces major enhancements to natural language
  comprehension and runtime reliability, featuring compound noun phrase preservation
  via InputParser5, autonomous disambiguation triage and phonetic prefix protection
  via EnvoyExecutionLayer5, strict non-biological domain shielding in EnvoyNormalizer5,
  and dual-key multi-alias persistence in RuntimeCore that completely eliminates
  repetitive interactive learning loops.

  Version 5.9.0 fully operationalizes the 4-Panel UI Suite (Duplicates, Triage,
  Navigation, and Terminal) with deterministic state clearance, preventing terminal
  deadlocks and securing host command isolation. Execution is driven centrally by
  sirius_orchestrator.py through an integrated single-process IPC Daemon running
  natively on port 8080.

  The system operates entirely on the user's device without cloud dependencies or
  external data transmission. All modules adhere to strict security boundaries,
  customs validation through COLNIK-6.x, autonomous decision supervision via
  AUTONOMY-6.x, Guard resource monitoring, and auditable symbolic explainability
  with proof trees and evidence chains.
